========================================================================
                      FANDOMVERSE — FAN WORLD NEXUS
                                ReadMe.doc
========================================================================

PROJECT OVERVIEW
------------------------------------------------------------------------
FandomVerse_SourceCode (Fan World Nexus) is a dynamic, modern web application designed
as a comprehensive portal and hub for pop culture enthusiasts. It brings
together diverse fandoms across multiple categories including Anime,
Gaming, Movies, TV Shows, K-Pop, Comics, and Manga.

The application offers an engaging user experience with dynamic content
rendering, article bookmarking, shopping cart functionality, theme switching
(light/dark mode), media previews, character profiles, and interactive search.


PROJECT STRUCTURE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
FandomVerse/
├── index.html          # Main HTML markup and application entry point
├── data.json           # JSON catalog containing articles, merch, events, etc.
├── css/
│   └── styles.css      # Main stylesheet with layout, animations, & themes
├── js/
│   ├── data.js         # Data management and loading utility
│   └── main.js         # Core application logic, event handlers, & state
└── assets/             # Media assets (images, icons, video clips)


KEY FEATURES
------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Fandom Hubs & Categories:
   - Browse dedicated hubs for Anime, Gaming, Movies, TV Shows, K-Pop, 
     Comics, and Manga.

2. Dynamic Content Catalog:
   - Articles, character profiles, upcoming events, and official merch
     loaded directly from `data.json`.

3. Interactive Search & Filtering:
   - Real-time global search across all fandom topics and categories.

4. User Experience & Customization:
   - Bookmarking system for saving favorite articles/characters.
   - Shopping cart modal for merch items.
   - Light & Dark theme toggle with persistent user preferences.
   - Mobile-responsive navigation drawer and breadcrumbs.


GETTING STARTED
------------------------------------------------------------------------
To launch and run the project locally:

1. Open `index.html` directly in any modern web browser (Chrome, Firefox,
   Edge, Safari).
   OR
2. Serve the directory using any static web server solution:
   - Using Python:
       python -m http.server 8000
   - Using Node.js live-server / http-server:
       npx http-server .

3. Open your browser and navigate to:
   http://localhost:8000 (or the port provided by your server).


TECHNOLOGIES USED
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- HTML5 (Semantic elements, accessible modal controls, breadcrumbs)
- CSS3 (CSS Custom Properties, Flexbox, CSS Grid, Responsive Design)
- JavaScript (Vanilla ES6+, Async/Fetch API, LocalStorage integration)
- JSON (Structured data store for site content)


DOCUMENTATION & MAINTAINER NOTES
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Content updates can be managed by modifying `data.json`.
- Styles and themes are controlled via CSS custom properties in `css/styles.css`.
- Core interactive functions (cart, bookmarks, modals, theme toggles) are 
  maintained in `js/main.js`.

